            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 85-year-old female patient, admitted on 11 April 2000 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. She responded well to treatment with clear clinical improvement. She is discharged in stable condition and I recommend continuation of her inhaled maintenance therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
